From 89f042da8752fd671897e5b55089cc53ada8cd35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vrisan <vrisanshah@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:14:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phase-T-kids-fixes-and-parent-overhaul

Four separate asks, addressed in order.

1. 'Offline mode where is it' -- it was never actually missing. The
   infra was all there since the PWA phase (public/sw.js,
   lib/offline-queue.ts, <OfflineBanner />) but had zero discoverable
   entry point: the banner only renders while something is actively
   queued/syncing, so there was no way to learn the feature exists
   ahead of time, or to install the app. Added
   components/kids/OfflineReadingInfoCard.tsx to Kids Settings:
   explains what it does, shows live online/offline status, and
   surfaces the real browser install prompt (beforeinstallprompt) when
   supported.

2. Shop purchases (pets, avatar accessories, shelf themes) not
   appearing anywhere -- found the actual bug. Equipping writes to
   users.equipped_pet_id / equipped_avatar_accessory_id /
   equipped_shelf_theme_id (app/api/kids/shop/equip/route.ts), but
   grep confirmed literally nothing outside the shop page itself ever
   read those three columns back -- not the home page, not the shelf,
   nowhere. (Badges/titles are a completely separate system that
   already worked correctly -- this bug was specific to shop
   cosmetics.) New lib/equipped-cosmetics.ts resolves all three ids
   into their shop_items rows in one place; EquippedSlots now renders
   the pet + accessory right on the avatar on the home page, and the
   Shelf page shows a themed banner (color by rarity) when a shelf
   theme is equipped.

3. Nav had 17 links total -- 5 primary + 12 stuffed into a 'More'
   dropdown, and ALL 17 crammed into one horizontally-scrolling row on
   mobile. Trimmed to 6: Home/Shelf/Discover stay primary; Messages/
   Profile/Settings are the only things left in More (account-y
   utility links, not features). Every other link -- Challenges,
   Leaderboard, Reading Game, BookTok, Book Club, Pip, Shop, Trades,
   Buddy Reading, Writing, Cards, Events -- moved onto the home
   dashboard as three organized tile sections (Explore & Play,
   Friends & Sharing, Shop & Trade) instead of disappearing. Nothing
   lost, just relocated to where a dashboard tile fits better than a
   nav item.

4. Parent dashboard overhaul, per the ask: nicer overview cards (now
   show current book + progress, clickable through to a new detail
   page), a family-wide summary strip (total minutes/books/streak
   across all kids), and a genuinely new per-child page
   (/parent/child/[id]) with tabs: Overview (7-day activity chart,
   badges, writing competition submissions), Books (currently
   reading/finished with covers), Reading Time (day-by-day bars),
   Events (weekend event placements with rank), and Discover (their
   want-to-read queue).

   Found a real gap while building this: event_entries and
   user_badges only ever had a 'select own' RLS policy (auth.uid() =
   user_id) -- a parent querying either for their kid got zero rows
   back, silently, not an error. New migration
   028_parent_dashboard_overhaul.sql adds is_parent_of()-based
   parent-read policies for both, matching the existing pattern
   already used for reading_sessions/user_books/user_challenges.
   Without this migration the new Events tab and badge list on the
   detail page render empty even though the code is correct.

Branched on top of phase-Q (not main) since phase-Q already touched
app/parent/dashboard/page.tsx (added the AdSense placement) -- this
avoids a patch conflict on that file. Apply phase-Q before this one;
order relative to phase-R/phase-S doesn't matter, neither touches any
file this patch does.
